The comments added in the patch clarify that GPIO names are not guaranteed to be unique, and they also indicate that warnings will be issued if a name is reused for a GPIO line on a different GPIO chip. This documentation helps developers understand the behavior of the functions and the implications of using non-unique names, thus mitigating confusion and potential errors in the code.


